    <mxCell id="me1" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=none;startArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="m_br1" target="m_br2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="me2" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=none;startArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="m_er1" target="m_er2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="me3" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=none;startArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="m_br1" target="m_er1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="me4" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=none;startArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="m_br2" target="m_er2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="me5" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=none;startArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="m_br1" target="m_er2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="me6" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=none;startArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="m_br2" target="m_er1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="mesh_note" value="6 pairs × 2 address families&lt;br&gt;= 12 iBGP sessions total" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="2330" y="455" width="310" height="44" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>

    <mxCell id="p_ospf" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="1700" y="590" width="960" height="440" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="p_ospf_txt" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;OSPF + BFD — one area, two instances, dual-stack&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;OSPFv2 instance &lt;b&gt;core&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp;area &lt;b&gt;bb&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; = 0.0.0.0 &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; OSPFv3 instance &lt;b&gt;core6&lt;/b&gt; area &lt;b&gt;bb6&lt;/b&gt; = 0.0.0.0&lt;br&gt;router-id = the &lt;b&gt;v4 loopback&lt;/b&gt; in BOTH instances (an OSPFv3 router-id is still 32-bit — an identifier, not an address)&lt;br&gt;Costs are IDENTICAL in both families, so a single link failure moves both or neither — never debug a failure twice.&lt;br&gt;Enabled on: lo0 (passive) · tun-bb / tun-wan1 / tun-wan2 (ptp) · ether3 (ptp) · ether4 (passive, customer-facing)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;BR↔BR backbone&lt;/b&gt; · cost 5 &amp;nbsp; · hello 5s / dead 20s &amp;nbsp;· BFD 200ms × 3 → detect ~600ms &amp;nbsp;(was 20s)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;wan1 tunnels&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;· cost 10 &amp;nbsp;· hello 5s / dead 20s &amp;nbsp;· BFD 300ms × 4 → detect ~1.2s &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(was 20s)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;wan2 tunnels&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;· cost 100 · hello 10s / dead 40s · BFD 1s × 5 &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ detect ~5s &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(was 40s)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;er1 ↔ er2 xc&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;· cost 1 &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;· default 40s dead &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;· BFD 100ms × 3 → detect ~300ms &amp;nbsp;(was 40s)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;WAN preference is expressed &lt;b&gt;only&lt;/b&gt; as OSPF cost — never in BGP, never in a name. Promoting wan2 is a two-line change.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;BFD is additive.&lt;/b&gt; /routing/bfd/configuration only PERMITS a session; use-bfd=yes on the OSPF interface-template is&lt;br&gt;what asks for one. If a BFD session never establishes, the network behaves exactly as it did before BFD existed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Default is DENY&lt;/b&gt; — ether1 (upstream) is simply absent from the menu and ether4 carries an explicit forbid-bfd=yes,&lt;br&gt;so neither an upstream nor a customer can ever negotiate BFD with us. OSPFv2 and OSPFv3 build their own sessions&lt;br&gt;per link and inherit the same class timers (the config entries match on interface, not family). BFD is UDP/3784,&lt;br&gt;already covered by in-interface-list=tunnels in the input chain, in both families.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;WireGuard interfaces never go down on their own&lt;/b&gt; — OSPF hellos plus BFD are the only liveness detector here." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="1716" y="608" width="930" height="410" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>

    <mxCell id="p_wg" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="1700" y="1060" width="960" height="470" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="p_wg_txt" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;WireGuard overlay — 9 point-to-point tunnels&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;MTU 1360 (worst underlay − 60) · MSS clamp 1320 · pre-shared key on every peer · persistent-keepalive 25s&lt;br&gt;allowed-address = 0.0.0.0/0,::/0 everywhere — routing is OSPF&#39;s job, not WireGuard&#39;s (::/0 is mandatory for v6)&lt;br&gt;naming = the FAR END, local view: on er1 the tunnel to br1 over wan1 is &lt;b&gt;wg-br1-wan1&lt;/b&gt;; on br1 it is &lt;b&gt;wg-er1-wan1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;br1↔er1 wan1 | .192 ↔ .193 | 2001:db8:0:30::0/127 | er1:51001 → br1:51821 | cost 10 | BFD 300ms×4&lt;br&gt;br1↔er1 wan2 | .194 ↔ .195 | 2001:db8:0:30::2/127 | er1:51101 → br1:51921 | cost 100 | BFD 1s×5&lt;br&gt;br1↔er2 wan1 | .196 ↔ .197 | 2001:db8:0:30::4/127 | er2:51001 → br1:51822 | cost 10 | BFD 300ms×4&lt;br&gt;br1↔er2 wan2 | .198 ↔ .199 | 2001:db8:0:30::6/127 | er2:51101 → br1:51922 | cost 100 | BFD 1s×5&lt;br&gt;br2↔er1 wan1 | .200 ↔ .201 | 2001:db8:0:30::8/127 | er1:51002 → br2:51821 | cost 10 | BFD 300ms×4&lt;br&gt;br2↔er1 wan2 | .202 ↔ .203 | 2001:db8:0:30::a/127 | er1:51102 → br2:51921 | cost 100 | BFD 1s×5&lt;br&gt;br2↔er2 wan1 | .204 ↔ .205 | 2001:db8:0:30::c/127 | er2:51002 → br2:51822 | cost 10 | BFD 300ms×4&lt;br&gt;br2↔er2 wan2 | .206 ↔ .207 | 2001:db8:0:30::e/127 | er2:51102 → br2:51922 | cost 100 | BFD 1s×5&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;br1↔br2 bbone&lt;/b&gt;| .160 ↔ .161 | 2001:db8:0:10::0/127 | br1:51102 ↔ br2:51101 | cost 5 &amp;nbsp;| BFD 200ms×3&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;PORT SCHEME&lt;/b&gt; — the BR listen port is what selects which ER WAN the outer packet leaves by:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;BR listens &lt;b&gt;5182x&lt;/b&gt; = wan1 side, &lt;b&gt;5192x&lt;/b&gt; = wan2 side &amp;nbsp;(x = ER index) &amp;nbsp;· backbone: BR listens 51100 + far BR index&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ER listens &lt;b&gt;5100x&lt;/b&gt; = wan1 side, &lt;b&gt;5110x&lt;/b&gt; = wan2 side &amp;nbsp;(x = BR index)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ER mangle marks the WG outer packet: UDP dst 51820-51829 → via-wan1 &amp;nbsp;· 51920-51929 → via-wan2&lt;br&gt;wan2 is CGNAT&#39;d 5G: no inbound port exists, so the &lt;b&gt;ER always initiates&lt;/b&gt; — endpoint-address is set on the ER side only.&lt;br&gt;Private keys live in keys.json (gitignored), generated once and never regenerated." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="1716" y="1078" width="930" height="440" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>

    <mxCell id="p_addr" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="1700" y="1560" width="960" height="510" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="p_addr_txt" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Addressing plan, origination and RPKI · AS64500&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;allocated&lt;/b&gt;: 203.0.113.0/24 (ARIN) · 2001:DB8::/40 (ARIN) &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;announced&lt;/b&gt;: 203.0.113.0/24 · &lt;b&gt;2001:DB8::/42&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;.0/25&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;customer home, pfSense VIPs &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ v6 2001:DB8:1::/48&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;.128/27&lt;/b&gt; remote-site delegations (sites: [] — none live yet)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;.160/28&lt;/b&gt; BR↔BR backbone /31s &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ v6 2001:DB8:0:10::/60&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;.176/28&lt;/b&gt; remote-site tunnel /31s &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ v6 2001:DB8:0:20::/60&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;.192/27&lt;/b&gt; BR↔ER tunnel /31s (16) &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ v6 2001:DB8:0:30::/60 &amp;nbsp;(/127s, RFC 6164)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;.224/28&lt;/b&gt; ER xc + customer transit &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ v6 2001:DB8:0:40::/60&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;.240/28&lt;/b&gt; loopbacks &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ v6 2001:DB8:0:0::/60 &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(br → ::b1/::b2 · er → ::e1/::e2)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why /42 and not /40:&lt;/b&gt; 2001:DB8:FC::/46 is reserved for AWS BYOIP and is deliberately OUTSIDE the announced&lt;br&gt;aggregate, because AWS originates it (AS14618 / AS16509), not us. The BRs hold the announced aggregate as a&lt;br&gt;blackhole at distance 254 — if that anchor covered the AWS range, internal traffic to our own AWS /48s would&lt;br&gt;match it and be dropped while the rest of the internet reached them fine. One DFZ entry, exactly like the /40.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;RPKI ROAs — all of these are required&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2001:DB8::/40 &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;— AS64500 — maxLength 40 &amp;nbsp;(keeps the unannounced rest of the /40 un-hijackable)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2001:DB8::/42 &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;— AS64500 — maxLength 42 &amp;nbsp;(without this the /42 is INVALID, not Unknown — worse)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2001:DB8:FC::/46 &amp;nbsp;— AS14618 &amp;nbsp;— maxLength 48 &amp;nbsp;(AWS BYOIP)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2001:DB8:FC::/46 &amp;nbsp;— AS16509 &amp;nbsp;— maxLength 48 &amp;nbsp;(AWS BYOIP — the ASN is region-dependent, so BOTH)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;203.0.113.0/24 &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;— AS64500 — maxLength 24 &amp;nbsp;(the v4 equivalent)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;DNS · example.net&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp;bare router name → loopback · interface addrs → {interface}.{router}.{site}.example.net&lt;br&gt;No DNS names in router configs — BGP, OSPF and anchor-guard use literal IPs, so a DNS outage cannot affect routing.&lt;br&gt;The WAN PTRs the world sees in a traceroute (198.51.100.57, 198.51.100.200) are set in the provider panel." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="1716" y="1578" width="930" height="480" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>

    <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;LEGEND&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&quot;#d79b00&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━━&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; eBGP to upstream (AS64515 / AS65473)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&quot;#9673a6&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━━&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; WireGuard tunnel carrying OSPFv2 + OSPFv3 + BFD (solid = wan1 / backbone, dashed = wan2)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&quot;#b85450&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;┅┅&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; eBGP to customer pfSense (AS65010 / AS65011)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&quot;#6c8ebf&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;┅┅&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; iBGP, loopback ↔ loopback (drawn as the inset mesh, top right — it overlays every link below and is not tied to any one of them)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━━&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; wired L2 / physical" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="200" y="2130" width="2460" height="72" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>

  </root>
</mxGraphModel>
</diagram></mxfile>